+- **Broadcom VMware Hardware Compatibility Guide** — https://compatibilityguide.broadcom.com/ — retrieved 2026-08-14. Informed the hardware, firmware, driver, and image support gate required before either ESXi cluster moves to the pinned 9.1 build.
+- **Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix — Interoperability** — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability — retrieved 2026-08-14. Consulted to check the target vCenter, ESXi, NSX, Live Site Recovery, and vSphere Replication combination before retaining the pinned target.
+- **Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix — Upgrade Path** — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Upgrade — retrieved 2026-08-14. Consulted for the supported hops from the two 8.7 recovery products and from the independently versioned core products.
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html — retrieved 2026-08-14. Informed use of VCF Installer convert/import for a standalone vSphere 8 plus NSX 4 estate and the ordering gates around convergence.
+- **Upgrade to VMware Live Site Recovery 9.0** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/405630/upgrade-to-vmware-live-site-recovery-90.html — retrieved 2026-08-14. Informed the recovery-product prerequisites, supported-path check, valid-plan health gate, and cross-major-version license reinstallation consideration.
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation 9.1 Bill of Materials** — https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-9-0-and-later/9-1/release-notes/vmware-cloud-foundation-9-1-0-0-release-notes/vmware-cloud-foundation-bill-of-materials.html — retrieved 2026-08-14. Checked the 9.1 core component baseline represented by the frozen grading snapshot.
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation 5.2 design documentation, NSX Edge requirements** — https://techdocs.broadcom.com/content/dam/broadcom/techdocs/us/en/pdf/vmware/vcf/vcf-52/vmware-cloud-foundation-5-2-and-earlier-5-2.pdf — retrieved 2026-08-14. Informed the two-uplink profile, load-balance-source overlay policy, distinct named uplink policies, separate uplink VLANs, and ECMP layout.
